    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I don't think that would be a good idea. As of now, there are two dependencies depending on it, there might be more in the future (if we introduce new dependencies or some dependencies introduce it, or even dependencies of dependencies).\r\n[Shipjs seems to rely on the fact that it can ignore errors](https://github.com/algolia/shipjs/blob/96d6ff22214849b7c0c665b3d104b00ded43b38a/packages/shipjs-lib/src/lib/git/getCommitBodies.js#L5), so there is a risk of enabling it globally breaks the release scripts. Nor safe now, or the future.\r\n\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nyarn why shelljs\r\nyarn why v1.22.10\r\n[1/4] 🤔  Why do we have the module \"shelljs\"...?\r\n[2/4] 🚚  Initialising dependency graph...\r\nwarning Resolution field \"algoliasearch@3.35.0\" is incompatible with requested version \"algoliasearch@^3.35.1\"\r\n[3/4] 🔍  Finding dependency...\r\n[4/4] 🚡  Calculating file sizes...\r\n=> Found \"shelljs@0.8.3\"\r\ninfo Has been hoisted to \"shelljs\"\r\ninfo This module exists because it's specified in \"devDependencies\".\r\ninfo Disk size without dependencies: \"316KB\"\r\ninfo Disk size with unique dependencies: \"452KB\"\r\ninfo Disk size with transitive dependencies: \"1.43MB\"\r\ninfo Number of shared dependencies: 11\r\n=> Found \"shipjs-lib#shelljs@0.8.4\"\r\ninfo This module exists because \"shipjs#shipjs-lib\" depends on it.\r\ninfo Disk size without dependencies: \"316KB\"\r\ninfo Disk size with unique dependencies: \"452KB\"\r\ninfo Disk size with transitive dependencies: \"1.43MB\"\r\ninfo Number of shared dependencies: 11\r\n=> Found \"@storybook/core#shelljs@0.8.4\"\r\ninfo This module exists because \"@storybook#html#@storybook#core\" depends on it.\r\ninfo Disk size without dependencies: \"348KB\"\r\ninfo Disk size with unique dependencies: \"484KB\"\r\ninfo Disk size with transitive dependencies: \"1.46MB\"\r\ninfo Number of shared dependencies: 11\r\n✨  Done in 1.08s.\r\n```",
    "commit_id": "fd82083328836ebfd777833ee45b9974672b8baf",
    "created_at": "2021-07-15T17:06:38Z",
